  "text": "Hiking - Visit Madeira | Madeira Islands Tourism Board official website Madeira Hiking Surprise yourself at every step with the exuberant scenery of this archipelago. Currently in Hiking Classified Walking Routes Where to book Other activities Frequently Asked Questions The thrill of hiking in Madeira's trails An ideal destination for hiking lovers. Mountains, ocean, green forests, waterfalls and viewpoints: the archipelago's natural wealth makes hiking in Madeira unforgettable and invigorating. Ready for a walk? Explore all the Official Hiking Trails Open PR1 - Vereda do Areeiro Open PR 1.1 - Vereda da Ilha Open PR 1.2 - Vereda do Pico Ruivo Restricted PR 1.3 - Vereda da Encumeada Open PR 2 - Vereda do Urzal Open PR 3 - Vereda do Burro Open PR 3.1 - Caminho Real do Monte Restricted PR 4 - Levada do Barreiro Open PR 5 - Vereda das Funduras Open PR 6 - Levada das 25 Fontes Open PR 6.1 - Levada do Risco Open PR 6.2 - Levada do Alecrim Open PR 6.3 - Vereda da Lagoa do Vento Open PR 6.4 - Levada Velha do Rabaçal Open PR 6.5 - Vereda do Pico Fernandes Open PR 6.6 - Vereda do Túnel do Cavalo Open PR 6.8 - Levada do Paul II - Um caminho para todos Closed PR 7 - Levada do Moinho Restricted PR 8 - Vereda da Ponta de São Lourenço Open PR 9 - Levada do Caldeirão Verde Open PR 9.1 - Levada do Caldeirão Verde - um caminho para todos Open PR 10 - Levada do Furado Open PR 11 - Vereda dos Balcões Restricted PR 12 - Caminho Real da Encumeada Open PR 13 - Vereda do Fanal Open PR 13.1 - Vereda da Palha Carga Open PR 14 - Levada dos Cedros Open PR 15 - Vereda da Ribeira da Janela Open PR 16 - Levada Fajã do Rodrigues Open PR 17 - Caminho do Pináculo e Folhadal Open PR 18 - Levada do Rei Open PR 19 - Caminho Real do Paul do Mar Closed PR 20 - Vereda do Jardim do Mar Open PR 21 - Caminho do Norte Open PR 22 - Vereda do Chão dos Louros Closed PR 27 - Glaciar de Planalto Closed PR 28 - Levada da Rocha Vermelha Open PS PR 1 - Vereda do Pico Branco e Terra Chã Open PS PR 2 - Vereda do Pico do Castelo Closed PS PR 3 - Levada do Pico do Castelo Current State of the Classified Walking Routes Before putting on your hiking boots, there's something you must do: make sure that the trail you have in mind is ready to be explored. This map shows you the current state of the classified walking routes - those that are open, those with some restrictions, and those inaccessible. Avoid surprises on the ground and make sure that every step is taken in the right direction. Learn, step by step, how to book your walks through the Simplifica portal. Watch video Access Conditions From January 1, 2026, access to the classified trails of the Autonomous Region of Madeira follows new rules: Access fee 4.5€ – for the general public and visitors accompanied by tourism animation companies (RNAVT and RNAAT) without a protocol with IFCN. 3€ – for visitors accompanied by tourism animation companies (RNAVT and RNAAT) that have a protocol with IFCN. Reservations are mandatory and continue to be made through the SIMplifica portal, where visitors choose their entry time according to the available 30-minute slots. For more information, consult the document issued by IFCN on the New Fees and Prices Model for 2026 or visit the institution’s website . Full List of Trails Check here the full list of trails classified by the Institute of Forests and Nature Conservation (IFCN). View Where to book Explore Nature Caminho do Lombinho Maiata de Baixo Porto da Cruz CCI 206 | 9225-190 Porto da Cruz (+351) 964 851 693 Email Website Find out more Hit the Road Rua Quinta Calaça, 3, Apartamentos do Mar, 217 |  9000-108 Funchal (+351) 969 466 359 Email Website Find out more Madeira With Linda Estrada Monumental, 520 | 9000-236 Funchal (+351) 918 959 190 Email Website Find out more Levata Tour Caminho do Barreiro 5 | 9350-135 Ribeira Brava (+351) 963 457 080 Email Find out more Adventure Kingdom Av Arriaga, 75 | Centro Comercial Marina Shopping, Loja 214 | 9000-533 Funchal (+351) 968 101 870 Email Find out more LokoLoko Rua D. Francisco Santana - Hotel Galosol | 9125-031 Caniço (+351) 291 939 191 Email Find out more Profetas D'Êxito Rua Jorge de Freitas, 23 | 9400-240 Porto Santo (+351) 961 183 989 Email Website Find out more Other activities Nature Activities Bike Tour Looking for a Bike Tour in Madeira? Exploring Madeira's trails by bike is one of the best ways to discover the natural landscapes of the archipelago. Read more Nature Activities Canyoning Madeira Canyoning? Discover Madeira's watercourses and immerse yourself in Nature! Read more Nature Activities Trail Running Madeira Trail Running? Enjoy the opportunity of running in mountain areas accompanied by exuberant and always surprising natural landscapes. Read more Nature Activities Climbing Looking for Madeira Climbing? Rugged cliffs, with the ocean as a backdrop, are the perfect scenery for an adrenaline-packed climbing experience in Madeira. Read more Nature Activities Bird Watching Bird Watching Madeira is the best opportunity to contemplate sea and land species, some of which rare, in preserved and highly respected ecosystems. Read more Nature Activities Nordic Walking Nordic Walking Madeira allows walkers to discover quiet mountain trails and thus access places of unequalled interest in the heart of the island. Read more Nature Activities Coasteering Coasteering Madeira? Walking, swimming, climbing, rappelling and jumping into water: all this in a single activity. Discover natural wonders of the island. Read more Nature Activities Madeira tours Madeira Tours? Discover the archipelago's natural secrets accompanied by expert guides. Read more Nature Activities Paragliding Exceed your limits and dare to Paragliding Madeira. Hovering over Madeira's mountains and its coastline is a vibrant and always very surprising activity. Read more Nature Activities Golf Golf in Madeira offers ideal conditions for pleasant practice at all times of the year, where tranquillity and natural beauty reign. Read more Venture out on our trails! FIND OUT MORE Faça aqui download APP Prociv Madeira Disponível para iOS e Android FAZER DOWNLOAD Frequently Asked Questions Is it mandatory to book hikes in Madeira? Yes. Access to all classified walking trails (PR) in Madeira requires a prior time reservation through the SIMplifica digital platform before starting your hike. Booking is mandatory for individual visitors, groups, and participants within tourism companies. How much does it cost to hike the official trails? In 2026, the fee applicable to classified hiking trails (PR) is generally €4.50 per person. We recommend consulting the specific page of each trail on Visit Madeira, where you can check the applicable fee and obtain further information regarding access and visiting conditions. Who has to pay the fee? Are there exemptions? The fee applies to all visitors using classified walking trails (PR). Residents of the Autonomous Region of Madeira are exempt from payment. Other specific conditions should be consulted in the current regulations . Where and how do I make a reservation? Reservations for official walking trails (PR) can only be made online via SIMplifica , the digital services portal of the Regional Government of Madeira. Payment must be made in advance, as internet coverage in mountainous areas may be limited. Which trails require mandatory booking? All classified walking trails (PR) in Madeira require a reservation. This includes official levadas and paths, such as: PR1 – Pico do Areeiro PR1.2 – Vereda do Pico Ruivo PR6 – Levada das 25 Fontes PR8 – Ponta de São Lourenço The full and updated list of trails is available on the hiking page of this website. What happens if I enter a PR trail without a valid reservation? Entering a classified walking trail (PR) without a reservation is an infraction. Visitors may be asked to leave the trail to regularise the situation, and under current regulations, the infraction may result in a fine Where can I check if a trail is open or closed? The updated status of classified walking trails (PR) can be checked on the official Visit Madeira website and the channels of the Institute of Forests and Nature Conservation (IFCN) . Each trail is identified as: Open Restricted Closed It is recommended to check the trail status before hiking, as conditions may change due to weather or safety factors. Keep in Touch @visitmadeira Subscribe to our newsletter and be surprised with every issue. email I unequivocally authorise the processing of these personal data in order to receive information regarding destination Madeira, offers, campaigns and other exclusive commercial messages from Visit Madeira, in accordance with the terms and conditions of the Privacy Policy of the Madeira Promotion Bureau.",
